From 7993622cdca8ff36f063d98fdc1ddf88cb8c443b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:38:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Headunit Server: a Connection Method, and on the phone's
 hotspot wait for WiFi

Headunit Server now asks which network the phone and the unit share:
Phone hotspot, Unit hotspot or Shared WiFi (Basic tab, Auto mode only).
Shared WiFi is the default and changes nothing; Unit hotspot is the
default for a unit with "Auto-Enable Hotspot" on, which now sits under it.

On the phone's hotspot:
- NetworkDiscovery skips its sweep while the unit is on no WiFi network,
  instead of probing other interfaces; the loop itself is untouched, and
  joining the hotspot already kicks a sweep at once.
- Connect over WiFi, with no WiFi joined, asks for a WiFi scan (or the
  WiFi panel when WiFi is off) and waits up to 60 s for a join, rescanning
  every 35 s, with Cancel in the main button's place. It then starts the
  search it always started. On WiFi, or with the unit's own access point
  up, it does exactly what it did before.
- The WiFi line on the main card stays, and now shows only here.
- An optional automatic scan (off by default) while the home is on screen
  and no WiFi is joined: at once, every 35 s for two minutes, then once a
  minute, within Android's four scans in two minutes.

The separate Scan WiFi button is gone: the main button does its job. The
main button drops its icon on a card too narrow for icon and label.

Rules are pure and unit-tested (HeadunitServerNetwork,
HomeWifiStatusPolicy). HomeWifiStatusLayoutTest lays the real home out in
all 26 locales on the narrowest screens and on 1920x720, day and dark,
connected, not connected, WiFi off, scanning and waiting;
HeadunitServerNetworkSettingRowTest checks the setting's labels in every
locale. Manual, Helper and Native are untouched.

